{"adjusted_val_bpb": 1.1017324568736933, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["Integrity: no problems. The diff changes one line in get_weight_decay. Weight decay now follows get_lr_multiplier(progress) instead of a linear (1 - progress) decay. It does not touch the metric, the data, the seed lines, the evaluation call, the summary printing or the prepare.py import.", "Bugs: none that would make the result meaningless. get_lr_multiplier is an existing schedule function that takes the same progress argument. One difference from before: with warmup or warmdown, weight decay now also ramps up from zero during warmup and holds at full strength through the flat phase.", "The z value can't be recomputed: there is only one candidate run and one incumbent run, so the numbers give no variance. The harness's z = -0.053 implies a noise sigma of about 0.0075 (0.0004 / 0.053). Its sign is correct: the candidate (1.1017) is 0.0004 worse than the incumbent (1.1013), which is well within noise.", "Claims: the numbers back the provisional reject. The candidate shows no improvement, and the change is not simpler than the incumbent."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Make Muon weight decay follow the LR multiplier (flat for the first half, then linear to 0) instead of decaying linearly over all of training.", "edit_class": "schedule", "flags": [], "gpu": 0, "idea_id": "i011", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 1.1013252182713982, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 1.1013252182713982, "n": 1}, "job_id": "1794427013_SS_06_candidate_6_cc7ccedf", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0589276, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0589276, "latency_s": 3.4202861208468676, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "coder", "served_model": "sonnet", "tokens_in": 14996, "tokens_out": 408}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.022090199999999997, "cost_usd_plan": 0.022090199999999997, "latency_s": 8.010105643421412